CORE dfcc-only
weak.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract function/contract _ --static-array
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum.*: FAILURE$
^\[function\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 7 dereference failure: pointer outside object bounds in x\[\(signed long int\)3\]: FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A separately named contract with a smaller minimum cannot justify the wrapped
implementation's static-bound access optimization: the wrapped
implementation's static-array precondition fails, and the access beyond the
contract's two elements keeps its ordinary pointer check.
